table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is  done.</p>  Example: She strongly voiced her concerns.</br> How did she voice her concerns? Strongly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This time I promise to act more enthusiastically! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Is it fair to say the last time you dated you were inadequately prepared to meet the girl? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding -ly to an adjective:</br> definite \u2192 definitely </br>         \t absolute \u2192 absolutely </p> Some adverbs are formed by adding -ally</br> Example:  enthusiastic \u2192  enthusiastically</p>  These adverbs can come after the direct object or after the  verb if there isn't any direct object."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blind date"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "going out with someone you have never seen in person before"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter, do you think you're ready to try the blind date thing again?  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about a blind date."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wavy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "curly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love her wavy hair."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "well-dressed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes someone who has good clothes that are suited to the person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: 